= Product overview

The application lets a user browse regional map data, explore network records and inspect project areas. It opens with a region overview, navigation controls, map layer settings and region-specific network context. Toronto and New York are selected from the left sidebar. Projects are selected from a dropdown that retains the configured project names. A region change reloads the page with the chosen region in its URL.

The project is local-first for its catalog and prepared datasets. The browser still needs internet access for the map style and tiles, terrain tiles and location search. The local Python service and SQLite database are required; serving the static files alone does not provide the region API.

The REGION dropdown shows the current region and lets users select another with a pointer or keyboard. The picker resolves catalog state through a view-model. A stalled catalog request is cancelled after eight seconds, and the startup screen offers a reload retry. Optional web fonts load without blocking the viewer; if application modules fail or startup remains stuck, the page offers a retry.

The database maintains Toronto network locations and New York reservations as individual records with their original details and coordinates. Map network data is assembled from these records. Existing databases are upgraded at startup without deleting project memberships. Refreshing changed regional input files replaces that region's imported network records; the viewer does not provide an interface for editing their details.

